  "english": "2. Sunday, Tone 4 [BK / Tone 2 Plagal]. Fourth. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 3 [GD / Tone 2]: \"We glorify You\" (Paravoremk zkez). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 4 [BK]: \"Christ is risen\" (Kristos yaryav).\n\n3. Monday, Tone 5 [GD / Tone 3]. Saint Andrew the General and his army, etc.\n\n4. Tuesday, Tone 6 [GK / Tone 3 Plagal]. Saint Adrian and his wife Anatolia, etc. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 6 [GK]: \"To You, O God\" (Ar kez astvats).\n\n5. Wednesday, Tone 7 [DZ / Tone 4]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] of Repentance Tone 4 [BK]: \"O God of our fathers\" (Vor hartsyn merots astvats).\n\n6. Thursday, Tone 8 [DK / Tone 4 Plagal]. Saints Abraham and Khoren, Cosmas and Damian, and the martyr Astvatsatur. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 8 [DK]: \"Who with wondrous\" (Vor zhrashapar).\n\n8. Saturday, Tone 2 [AK / Tone 1 Plagal]. Feast of the Nativity of the Holy Mother of God.\n\n9. Sunday, Tone 3 [BD / Tone 2]. Fifth. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 6 [GK]: \"Ineffable\" (Anchareli). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [BD]: \"At the grave\" (I gerezman) and \"They came to the tomb\" (Ekin i gerezman). Carnival [Barekendan] of the Fast of the Holy Cross.\n\n10. Monday, Tone 4 [BK / Tone 2 Plagal]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] of Repentance Tone 4 [BK]: \"Lord God of our fathers\" (Ter astvats hartsyn merots).\n\n16. Sunday, Tone 2 [AK / Tone 1 Plagal]. Exaltation of the Holy Cross. Up to the tenth Sunday, see in order the First Volume, keeping the order of this place.\n\n23. Sunday, Tone 1 [AD / Tone 1]. Second [after Cross]. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 1 [AD]: \"With the women\" (Ynt kanaysn). Carnival [Barekendan] of the Holy Cross of Varag.\n\n24. Monday, Tone 2 [AK / Tone 1 Plagal]. Fast. Saint Mamas, etc. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] Tone 1 [AD]: \"You, the righteous\" (Yzkez ardar).\n\n26. Wednesday, Tone 4 [BK / Tone 2 Plagal]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harst] of Repentance Tone 5 [GD]: \"Blessed and glorified art You, O Lord\" (Orhneal es ter ev paravoreal).\n\n30. Sunday, Tone 8 [DK / Tone 4 Plagal]. Third [after Cross]. Feast of the Holy Cross of Varag. The period of non-fasting is seven weeks. See the order in the First Volume.\n\nOctober 5.\n\n7. Sunday, Tone 7 [DZ / Tone 4]. Fourth. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [DZ]: \"The women anticipating\" (Kanantsn kanchelov) and \"The awesome\" (Ahagin).\n\n14. Sunday, Tone 6 [GK / Tone 3 Plagal]. Fifth. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [GK]: \"The divine\" (Zastvatsayin) and \"Your resurrection\" (Yzkoy harutyund).\n\n21. Sunday, Tone 5 [GD / Tone 3]. Sixth. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [GD]: \"The oil-bearers\" (Yughaber) and \"Today the resurrection\" (Aysor harutyun) and \"In the sign of the cross\" (I khachanish).",
